---
description: Guardrails for the live RPM Mentor Hub repository
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/RPM-LIVE-OPERATING-GUIDE.md` before making a plan or edit.

Use only the RPM Mentor Hub repository and its current `origin/main` baseline. The live app is deployed from Vercel and uses the standalone RPM Supabase project described in the guide. Do not substitute GKHQ, Split Decision, an old Lovable Cloud project, a preview URL, or a Google Sheet.

You may plan, branch, edit, test, and create local commits. You must not push, merge, deploy, modify Vercel settings, modify Supabase Auth/RLS/data, run production migrations, invite users, alter DNS, or expose/commit credentials unless the owner explicitly approves that exact action in the current request.

Treat `public.match_reports_cache` as the canonical live Match Report store. Google Sheets is only archive/backfill/rollback material. Do not use name-only matching for data changes. Do not run `supabase db push` against production: the live database has documented safety adjustments that must be preserved.

For every change, state the scope and acceptance criteria first. Keep the patch focused. Run the most relevant tests plus `npm run build` for build/runtime work and `git diff --check` before committing. Report failures honestly; never claim a deploy, database migration, or live verification from a local check.
